  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Steppin'** (1 review): Reviewer is pleased to hear Steppin' included on this recording [4]\n- **Tuesday Night's Squad** (1 review): Played as the encore, closing the show after the second disc's main set [2]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Kalen**: rare: 11 archived performances [6]\n- **Reunion**: rare: 6 archived performances [6]\n- **Bridge to 'Bama cont'd**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [6]\n- **Turn it Out cont'd**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [6]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **sl2002-02-23.c1000.flac16** (recommended): source not stated; 14 songs; 149 min; rated 4.5/5 by 4 [1]. Said about its sound: Reviewer describes the recording as crisp-sounding [4]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Topaz on tenor sax and Squantch on trombone joined the band for this song [1]\n- Cannonball featured guests: Topaz on tenor sax and Squantch on trombone [2]\n- Attendee recalls the Asheville Music Zone crowd being rowdy that night [5]\n- Attendee says the Topaz players, who sat in, performed solidly [5]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **sl2002-02-23.c1000.flac16**: taped by Cliff Lawless; transferred by Cliff Lawless; source: AKG C1000S (FOB, hypercard, DIN) > Denecke AD-20 > Sony TCD-D8 [1]. Also: Uploader admits the track splits on this upload are slightly off, since they didn't relisten before posting [3]",
